# Unit tests: Functions & Closures

Create a function called add with x, y:
    Return x + y

Assert(add(15, 25) is equal to 40, "Simple function call")

# Recursion
Create a function called fib with n:
    If n is at most 1:
        Return n
    Return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)

Assert(fib(0) is equal to 0, "Fibonacci 0")
Assert(fib(1) is equal to 1, "Fibonacci 1")
Assert(fib(7) is equal to 13, "Fibonacci 7")

# Closures
Create a function called make_adder with base:
    Create a function called inner with extra:
        Return base + extra
    Return inner

Set add10 to make_adder(10)
Assert(add10(5) is equal to 15, "Closure adder 1")
Assert(add10(20) is equal to 30, "Closure adder 2")

# Stateful closure
Create a function called accumulator with start:
    Set total to start
    Create a function called add_amount with amt:
        Increase total by amt
        Return total
    Return add_amount

Set acc to accumulator(100)
Assert(acc(50) is equal to 150, "Stateful closure first call")
Assert(acc(25) is equal to 175, "Stateful closure second call")
